# Cross-encoder resource grid, Milestone 2 remediation 2 (separate tokenization, bounded ONNX Runtime calls), 2026-09-13 11:51 +08, commit base 9085d0c plus working tree
# Machine: Apple M4, 16 GB, macOS 26.5.1; openjdk version "26.0.1" 2026-04-21
# Each case: a fresh child JVM, 'java -Xmx1g -cp <target/test-classes:target/classes:dependencies> project.stockrecommendationengine.rag.retrieval.CrossEncoderResourceProbe <modelDir> <maxLength> <batchSize> <unit> <chars> <passages> [threads]'
# wrapped in '/usr/bin/time -l'; a watchdog sampled the child's RSS every 0.2 s and would kill it above 4 GB (never triggered).
# The query and every passage are the same text: unit a = "a " repeated to <chars> characters, cjk = U+4E2D x <chars>, filing = a short question against <chars>-character filing-like passages.
# Two score() calls per JVM (call 1 includes warm-up). 'peak memory footprint' (bytes) is for the whole process: JVM, model, ONNX Runtime and tokenizer.

